\f0\fs24 \cf0 To run the Tribute wall:\
\
In Terminal:\
cd "/Users/ted/Desktop/Claude Results/tribute-wall"\
/usr/local/bin/npm start\
\
In Browser:\
Open http://localhost:3000 for the user site\
Or http://localhost:3000/admin.html for the admin site\
\
\
\
Deployment instructions:\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 This is a Node.js app, so deployment means running the server process continuously and routing traffic to it via your existing web server. Here are the two most common setups:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Option A \'97 Subdomain (easiest)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs26 \cf0 tribute.yourdomain.com
\f1\fs24  
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  your Node app on port 3000\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 1. Copy the app to your server\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs26 \cf0 scp -r "/Users/ted/Desktop/Claude Results/tribute-wall" user@yourserver:/var/www/tribute-wall\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Or use git. Exclude 
\f3\fs26 node_modules/
\f1\fs24 , 
\f3\fs26 data/
\f1\fs24 , and 
\f3\fs26 uploads/
\f1\fs24  \'97 recreate those on the server.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Install dependencies on the server\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs26 \cf0 cd /var/www/tribute-wall\
npm install --omit=dev\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Run with PM2 (keeps it alive across reboots)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs26 \cf0 npm install -g pm2\
pm2 start server.js --name tribute-wall\
pm2 save\
pm2 startup   # follow the printed command to enable on boot\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 4. Add an nginx reverse proxy block\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs26 \cf0 server \{\
    listen 80;\
    server_name tribute.yourdomain.com;\
\
    # Serve uploaded files directly (faster than Node)\
    location /uploads/ \{\
        alias /var/www/tribute-wall/uploads/;\
    \}\
\
    # Proxy everything else to Node\
    location / \{\
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;\
        proxy_http_version 1.1;\
        proxy_set_header Host $host;\
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';\
        # Allow large photo uploads (default nginx limit is 1MB)\
        client_max_body_size 50M;\
    \}\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Then add HTTPS via Certbot:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 certbot --nginx -d tribute.yourdomain.com\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Option B \'97 Subdirectory path\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs26 \cf0 yourdomain.com/tribute
\f1\fs24  
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  same server, path prefix\
This requires one small code change so the app knows it's mounted under 
\f3\fs26 /tribute
\f1\fs24 :\
The nginx block for Option B:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 # Inside your existing server \{\} block for yourdomain.com\
\
location /tribute/uploads/ \{\
    alias /var/www/tribute-wall/uploads/;\
\}\
\
location /tribute/ \{\
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000/tribute/;\
    proxy_set_header Host $host;\
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\
    client_max_body_size 50M;\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Start the app with the path prefix set:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 BASE_PATH=/tribute pm2 start server.js --name tribute-wall \\\
  --env BASE_PATH=/tribute\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Or set it permanently in a PM2 ecosystem file:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 // ecosystem.config.js\
module.exports = \{\
  apps: [\{\
    name: 'tribute-wall',\
    script: 'server.js',\
    env: \{ PORT: 3000, BASE_PATH: '/tribute' \}\
  \}]\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Two things to sort out before going live\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 1. Change the JWT secret and default password
\f1\b0 \
Set real values via environment variables \'97 never leave the defaults in production:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 JWT_SECRET=some-long-random-string pm2 start server.js --name tribute-wall\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Then log into the admin panel and change the 
\f3\fs26 admin
\f1\fs24  password immediately.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 2. Persistent data
\f1\b0 \
The 
\f3\fs26 data/
\f1\fs24  and 
\f3\fs26 uploads/
\f1\fs24  folders are what matters \'97 back them up regularly. If you ever redeploy the app code, leave those directories in place and they'll survive.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

